{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>If there be found in your midst.</b> After commanding the appointment of judges in every city to judge, each court over the people of its own city, he mentioned the case of one who serves idolatry, who is not tried in his own city but is tried in that city where he committed the act. And after that he mentioned the matter of a dispute between courts, which is likewise tried in another city — namely, <b>בַּמָּקוֹם אֲשֶׁר יִבְחַר ה׳</b> (Deuteronomy 17:8). And so too the matter of the rebellious elder." "<b>To transgress His covenant.</b> The covenant that He made regarding all the commandments — for indeed one who serves idolatry denies all the commandments and nullifies them."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:21:40.442657347Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}